{%- # CUSTOM: net-new snippet — renders one review card. Accepts explicit named params (not a bundled settings/block object) so it can be called either from a repeatable block (sections/custom-reviews.liquid) or from plain section settings (sections/custom-subscribe-benefits.liquid's single testimonial) without needing matching field ids in both places. Computes the card's data-tags attribute (merchant-entered comma tags + an auto "has_photos" tag when a photo is set) which assets/mo-review-filter.js reads to decide visibility per active filter pill. UPSTREAM risk LOW — no Horizon file touched. -%}
{%- # Params: name, location, meta_type ('subscriber' or 'professional'), duration, photo, rating, quote, tags (comma-separated string), shopify_attributes (optional, pass block.shopify_attributes when rendering from a block), badge_style (optional: 'auto' [default] shows a mint pill only for meta_type 'professional' and mono meta text for 'subscriber'; 'pill' always renders a mint pill, used by custom-subscribe-benefits.liquid per its Figma reference) -%}
{%- comment -%}
  CUSTOM FIX (2026-07-17, per Kalvis + Figma node 633:591): `round: 1` alone
  drops the decimal for whole-number ratings (5 -> "5", not "5.0") — Liquid's
  round filter returns an Integer, not a Float, when the input is already a
  whole Integer (block.settings.rating can be, even with a 0.5 step range).
  `times: 1.0` coerces to Float first so round always keeps one decimal.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  CUSTOM FIX (2026-07-18, per Kalvis): filter pills' tag_key presets use
  underscores (e.g. "most_helpful", "lens_wearer") but a merchant typing tags
  naturally into this field (e.g. "Most Helpful") only had SPACES stripped
  here, not converted to underscores — "most helpful" -> "mosthelpful",
  which never matched "most_helpful", so no filter ever showed a narrowed
  result. Now strips underscores/hyphens too (on both this side and the
  filter pill's tag_key in custom-reviews.liquid) so "Most Helpful",
  "most_helpful", and "most-helpful" all normalize to the same string.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign shopify_attributes = shopify_attributes | default: ''
  assign badge_style = badge_style | default: 'auto'
  assign tags_final = tags | strip | downcase | remove: ' ' | remove: '_' | remove: '-'
  if photo != blank
    assign tags_final = tags_final | append: ',has_photos'
  endif
  assign tags_final = tags_final | split: ',' | join: ','
  assign rating_display = rating | times: 1.0 | round: 1
-%}
<article class="mo-reviews__card" data-tags="{{ tags_final }}" {{ shopify_attributes }}>
  <div class="mo-reviews__card-head">
    {%- if name != blank -%}
      <h3 class="mo-reviews__name mo-h4">{{ name | escape }}</h3>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if location != blank -%}
      <p class="mo-reviews__location mo-h4">{{ location | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if meta_type == 'professional' -%}
    <span class="mo-reviews__pro-badge mo-tag--sm">VERIFIED EYE CARE PROFESSIONAL</span>
  {%- elsif badge_style == 'pill' -%}
    <span class="mo-reviews__pro-badge mo-tag--sm">VERIFIED SUBSCRIBER</span>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      CUSTOM: added base .mo-tag (mono font-family + uppercase transform) alongside
      .mo-tag--sm (size override) — was missing, so this rendered in the body font
      instead of IBM Plex Mono (audit #13/#24, 2026-07-17).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="mo-reviews__meta mo-tag mo-tag--sm">
      VERIFIED SUBSCRIBER{% if duration != blank %} · {{ duration | escape | upcase }}{% endif %}
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if photo != blank -%}
    <div class="mo-reviews__photo">
      {{
        photo
        | image_url: width: 800
        | image_tag:
          widths: '400, 600, 800',
          loading: 'lazy',
          alt: photo.alt | default: name,
          class: 'mo-reviews__photo-img'
      }}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="mo-reviews__rating">
    <span class="mo-reviews__rating-value mo-h5">{{ rating_display }}</span>
    {%- render 'mo-stars', rating: rating -%}
  </div>

  {%- if quote != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      CUSTOM (2026-07-28, per Kalvis): quote text is CSS line-clamped (4
      lines mobile / 3 lines desktop — see .mo-reviews__quote in
      custom.css) with an always-rendered "Read more" toggle button below
      it. The button starts `hidden` (no-JS-safe default: a card whose
      quote actually fits within the clamp should never show a toggle
      that does nothing) and assets/mo-reviews-quote.js reveals it only
      once it confirms the text was actually truncated, then wires up the
      expand/collapse click.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="mo-reviews__quote mo-body-lg">&ldquo;{{ quote | escape }}&rdquo;</p>
    <button type="button" class="mo-reviews__quote-toggle" data-quote-toggle hidden aria-expanded="false">read more</button>
  {%- endif -%}
</article>
